<title>ISRAEL: Israel commercial banks lower prime rate.</title>
<headline>Israel commercial banks lower prime rate.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's commercial banks announced they were reducing the prime interest rate by 0.5 percentage point to an annualised 17.3 percent.</p>
<p>The lowering of the rate follows an earlier announcement by the central bank that it was lowering its key lending rate to commercial banks for September by 0.5 percentage point to an annualised 15.8 percent.</p>
<p>The new rate will come into force on August 29, the banks said.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211</p>
